{"name":"Playful Purple","hex":"#bfb9d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"playful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Enjoying play; sportive; prone to playing frequently, in the manner of a child or young pet (viz. puppy or kitten).","Funny; humorous; jesty; frolicsome; frisky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/playful"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Play (activity)","blocks":[{"text":"Play is a range of intrinsically motivated activities done for recreation. Play is commonly associated with children and juvenile-level activities, but may be engaged in at any life stage, and among other higher-functioning animals as well, most notably mammals and birds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Playfulness_by_Paul_Manship%2C_1912-1914_-_DSC03107.JPG/330px-Playfulness_by_Paul_Manship%2C_1912-1914_-_DSC03107.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Play_(activity)","wikidata":"Q1150958"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg/500px-July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg/1280px-July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg/500px-July_4th_Traditions_%287188250241%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"People having fun","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJuly_4th_Traditions_(7188250241).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg/500px-Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg/1280px-Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg/500px-Dreibeinlauf-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A three-legged race is a form of competition that requires cooperation with a partner. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADreibeinlauf-4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8